Menu="OtherSettings"
Title="Deadlock Guard"
Icon="shield"
---
<div id="deadlock-guard" class="dg-settings">
  <h2>Deadlock Guard <small>Beta · Unraid 7.3.x</small></h2>
  <p>Use the normal VMs, Docker and Dashboard controls. Starting a group member stops conflicting workloads first. Stopping a workload never starts another.</p>
  <div class="dg-notice"><strong>Coverage and setup</strong><p>Grouped VM starts from terminal commands, scripts and autostart are blocked. Disable autostart for those VMs. Docker CLI/API starts, restart policies, autostart and update/recreation starts bypass this plugin; disable automatic starts for grouped containers. This is not system-wide exclusivity.</p><p>GPU/PCI driver rebinding remains your responsibility. A failed handoff leaves stopped workloads stopped. Force-stop can lose unsaved data and is disabled by default.</p></div>
  <p id="dg-health" role="status">Loading integration status…</p>
  <div class="dg-actions"><button type="button" id="dg-check">Check integration and reconcile</button><button type="button" id="dg-reload">Reload configuration</button></div>
  <p id="dg-message" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
  <div id="dg-groups"></div>
  <div class="dg-actions"><button type="button" id="dg-add">Add exclusive group</button><button type="button" id="dg-save">Save groups</button></div>
  <h3>Workload status</h3><div id="dg-inventory"></div>
  <h3>Recent handoffs</h3><p>Accepted jobs continue after this page closes. History is kept in RAM until reboot (up to 200 completed jobs).</p><div id="dg-history"></div>
  <p><a href="https://github.com/ghaschel/unraid-deadlock-manager/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Support on GitHub Issues</a></p>
</div>
<script src="/plugins/deadlock-guard/javascript/settings.js" defer></script>
